() Tj T*
(During routine preparation of an IV analgesic dose for a post-operative patient,) Tj T*
(our pharmacy technician observed a visible dark brown fibrous particle suspended) Tj T*
(inside a sealed 10 mL vial of Morphine Sulfate Injection 10 mg/mL, batch) Tj T*
(MOR-2026-089. The particle measured approximately 3 mm in length.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The vial was immediately removed from use and quarantined. Upon inspection of) Tj T*
(the remaining vials from the same shipment, 3 additional vials showed similar) Tj T*
(particulate matter. A total of 6 vials from this batch have been quarantined.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The affected batch was received on 2026-01-28 and stored under recommended) Tj T*
(conditions \(15-25 degrees C, protected from light\). No other batches of this) Tj T*
(product are currently in use at our facility.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
50 176 Td
14 TL
(PATIENT IMPACT) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 176 Td
14 TL
() Tj T*
(The contaminated vial was identified before administration. No patient was) Tj T*
(harmed. However, given the critical nature of the product \(opioid injectable\),) Tj T*
(we consider this a HIGH patient safety risk and are requesting an urgent) Tj T*
(investigation and written response within 72 hours.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
